<title>USA: Giant seeks injunction to keep Visa program.</title>
<headline>Giant seeks injunction to keep Visa program.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON, D.C. 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Giant Food Inc said Monday it is seeking a temporary restraining order to prevent M&amp;T Bank of Buffalo, N.Y., from discontinuing a co-branded Visa program that gives rebates to Giant customers.</p>
<p>M&amp;T issues the Giant and Super G Visa cards, which pay users rebates through quarterly checks that apply only toward purchases at Giant stores.</p>
<p>M&amp;T wants to end the program Tuesday night, said Giant spokesman Barry Scher, &quot;because they say most people pay their accounts monthly and they're not making money on it.&quot;</p>
</text>
